= The Secretariat answers

By June the paper has done its work in Moscow, and the name of the work is fear. A General Secretary whose character has been described by the founder of the party himself, in words that many of the leaders have now read, cannot behave as if nothing had been said. Stalin does not deny that the notes exist. He does something cleverer: he says that a sick man's last words ought to be treated with respect, and then reads aloud from the places where they are hard on his rivals.

[? if testament_path = 1 : The Left Opposition, which has the paper from Radek, forces the question into the Politburo. Trotsky, who has the habit of being right at the wrong moment, speaks too long and too well, and Zinoviev and Kamenev, who have read their own October in Lenin's pages, find that they would rather not decide anything this month. ?]
[? if testament_path = 2 : The defenders of the NEP, with Bukharin in front, ask in the Politburo whether a party whose secretary governs by his appointments can still be called one that governs itself. Rykov and Tomsky do not speak; their silence is understood. Zinoviev and Kamenev, who had thought the quarrel was between Stalin and Trotsky, find it has a third side. ?]
[? if testament_path = 3 : Our newspaper's extracts are on every desk in Moscow, with the German press's commentary pinned to them. Nobody can say that the notes are a rumour, and nobody can say that they were released by the Russian party. The Comintern's executive is furious, and it is the Germans who are furious at. ?]

Stalin is, for the first time in his career, on the defensive. It is not the position he likes. He is a man who prefers to wait until he has the votes, and he is now being asked to wait without them. His apparatus responds as apparatuses do. The Secretariat's emissaries are sent to our district committees, with a list of questions about how a Russian paper reached Berlin, and who in the Zentrale allowed it. Moscow's trust in us falls [? if testament_path = 3 : by ten, and a payment promised for the summer is held back (one resource) ?][? if testament_path < 3 : by eight ?]. The Centre, our most loyal faction, rallies to the secretariat and gains four points of strength.

Whatever happens next in the Russian party, we are now part of it.

